   "text": {
    "L1": "The Sun is not the biggest star. It is an ordinary, medium-sized star in the Milky Way.",
    "L2": "Betelgeuse is hundreds of times wider than the Sun, but it is very far away. Distance changes how big a star looks.",
    "L3": "Our Earth is inside the solar system. The solar system is inside the Milky Way galaxy.",
    "L4": "A galaxy is a huge collection of billions of stars, together with gas and dust. Our Sun is one star in it, far from its centre.",
    "L5": "The universe contains billions of galaxies. We use light-years to describe these enormous distances.",
    "L6": "From a dark place such as Hanle, the Milky Way can appear as a faint, milky band. City lights can hide it.",
    "L7": "So our address in space is Earth, solar system, Milky Way, then universe. Put these in order."
   },
